@format 1
@id ui-event.7a1fe4211badc1c0
@title Active viewer media change
@section I. UI
@area UI event
@tabs Split, Edit, Convert, Audio, Merge, Funnel, Global interface
@event-ref cs|PMainWindow/PWindow.xaml.cs|PWindowWorkspaceAttach|pViewerActive|PViewerMediaChange|1
@entry input
@summary Attach media to the active flow or clear it on empty media; inactive lifecycle cleanup does not depend on this subscription.
@tag viewer media change
@tag PWindow
@alias owner = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PWindow
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow

[input] Active viewer media changed <input>
- Receive media status through the subscription installed for the active workspace @ owner.PWindowWorkspaceAttach
> media

[media] Does the status contain media info? <decision>
- Inspect the cargo passed to the window media handler @ owner.PWindowMediaHandle
? "Media info is present" > attach
? "Media info is empty" > clear

[attach] Attach active flow <process>
- Attach media information, source path, and zero start time to the active flow @ flow.PFlowAttach
> output

[clear] Clear active flow <process>
- Clear the active flow; repeated cleanup is harmless @ flow.PFlowClear
> output

[output] Active flow synchronized <output>
= The active flow matches its viewer. Inactive removals are synchronized directly by the tab lifecycle handler.
! Code binding: cs|PMainWindow/PWindow.xaml.cs|PWindowWorkspaceAttach|pViewerActive|PViewerMediaChange|1
